.TH EGGHEAD 5 "April 2026" "egghead 0.1.0" "Egghead Manual"
.SH NAME
egghead \- configuration file format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I ~/.config/egghead/config.yml
.SH DESCRIPTION
The egghead configuration file is a YAML document that controls
records location, LLM provider credentials, default model, and
web server settings.
.PP
The file location follows the XDG Base Directory specification,
defaulting to
.IR ~/.config/egghead/config.yml .
Override with the
.B EGGHEAD_CONFIG
environment variable or the
.B \-\-config
flag.
.SH FORMAT
.nf
records_dir: ~/.egghead

llm:
  - provider: anthropic
    api_key: sk-ant-...
  - provider: openai
    api_key: "{env:OPENAI_API_KEY}"
  - provider: custom
    name: local-llama
    base_url: http://localhost:11434/v1
    api_key: ollama

default_model: anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5

web:
  port: 4000
  host: localhost
  bind: 127.0.0.1
.fi
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B records_dir
Path to the records directory. Tilde expansion is supported.
Default: ~/.egghead
.TP
.B llm
List of LLM provider configurations. Each entry has:
.RS
.TP
.B provider
Provider name: anthropic, openai, google, or custom.
.TP
.B api_key
API key string, or an environment variable reference using
the \fB{env:VAR_NAME}\fR syntax.
.TP
.B base_url
(Optional) Base URL for custom OpenAI-compatible endpoints.
.TP
.B name
(Optional) Display name for custom providers.
.RE
.TP
.B default_model
Model ID in \fIprovider/model\fR format (e.g. anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5).
Used by the built-in Index agent. Other agents specify their own model
in their record frontmatter.
.TP
.B web.port
HTTP port for the web server. Default: 4000.
.TP
.B web.host
Hostname for URL generation. Default: localhost.
.TP
.B web.bind
Bind address. Use 0.0.0.0 for network access. Default: 127.0.0.1.
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLE REFERENCES
API keys can reference environment variables instead of storing
secrets in plaintext:
.PP
.nf
api_key: "{env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY}"
.fi
.PP
The variable is resolved at runtime. If the variable is not set,
the key is treated as nil.
.SH SEE ALSO
